        {
          "title": "Implement LRUCache",
          "status": "done",
          "model": "default",
          "mode": "auto",
          "worktree": false,
          "brief": "Implement an LRUCache class in lru.js with the following requirements:\n\n1. **O(1) Operations**: Implement get() and put() with constant time complexity using a Map and doubly-linked list.\n\n2. **Capacity & Eviction**: Support a capacity parameter. When full, evict the least recently used item before adding a new one. Both get() and put() should update recency.\n\n3. **TTL Support**: Add optional ttlMs parameter to the constructor. When set, entries expire after ttlMs milliseconds. Expired entries must never be returned from get() and should be cleaned up on access.\n\n4. **API**:\n   - constructor(capacity, ttlMs = null)\n   - get(key) - returns value or undefined; updates recency if found and not expired\n   - put(key, value) - adds/updates entry; evicts LRU if at capacity\n   - size() - returns current number of valid entries\n   - clear() - removes all entries\n\n5. **Thorough Tests** in a test file covering:\n   - Basic get/put operations\n   - Eviction order verification (oldest unused is evicted first)\n   - TTL expiration and never-return guarantee\n   - Edge case: get/put updates recency correctly\n   - Edge case: accessing an expired entry doesn't return it and cleans it\n   - Capacity boundary: fill to capacity, then add one more triggers eviction\n   - Multiple TTL entries with staggered expiration times\n   - Clear operation empties the cache\n\nImplement in pure JavaScript without external dependencies. Make the implementation efficient and the tests comprehensive.",
          "workerTools": [
            "report_progress",
            "report_progress",
            "report_outcome"
          ],
          "outcome": {
            "status": "success",
            "derived": false,
            "proof": [
              "tests*:pass"
            ],
            "risks": [
              "size() is O(n) when a TTL is set, because it sweeps expired entries. Without a TTL it is O(1).",
              "Expired entries occupy capacity until they are accessed or size() is called. Eviction takes the LRU entry whether or not it has expired.",
              "get() refreshes recency but not expiry. TTL counts from the last put() on the key, which is a design choice the spec left open."
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
